Modifications relative to upstream:

  1. Added --paddle-inference-engine {auto,paddle,onnxruntime}
     Lets the classic pipeline run on ONNX Runtime instead of paddle_static.
     On CPU and PP-OCRv6 this is 5-10x faster, and it avoids the oneDNN crash
     described below. "--paddle-inference-engine auto" (the default) prefers
     onnxruntime when it is installed.

  2. Added --paddle-no-mkldnn
     Disables oneDNN/MKL-DNN. The paddle_static + oneDNN path raises
         NotImplementedError: (Unimplemented) ConvertPirAttribute2RuntimeAttribute
         not support [pir::ArrayAttribute<pir::DoubleAttribute>]
         (at .../onednn_instruction.cc:116)
     on some paddlepaddle builds (reproduced with the nixpkgs 3.3.0 CPU wheel).
     Environment flags FLAGS_use_mkldnn=0 / FLAGS_enable_pir_api=0 do not help,
     because paddlex enables oneDNN explicitly in its runner.

  3. Added --paddle-det-limit-type and --paddle-det-limit-side-len
     PaddleX ships limit_type=min / limit_side_len=64 for the OCR pipeline,
     which effectively means "do not downscale": a 400 DPI page raster
     (3306x4678) is fed to the detector unchanged. Defaults are now
     max / 960, matching the values recommended by the PaddleOCR docs.

  4. __init__.py no longer depends on setuptools_scm; the version is read from
     package metadata.

  5. Model instances are cached per process
     Upstream called PaddleOCR(...) / PaddleOCRVL(...) once per page inside
     generate_hocr(), so every page paid the model load again (~1.8 s for
     PP-OCRv6 medium). _get_paddle_ocr()/_get_paddle_vl() now delegate to
     lru_cache'd builders keyed on the settings that actually change what gets
     loaded; each worker process therefore loads the models once.

  6. packaging: pyproject.toml rewritten (no setuptools_scm, PEP 639 license,
     optional extras), Nix expressions added under nix/.

Everything else - the hOCR generation, word box merging, polygon handling and
language mapping - is unchanged upstream code.

Upstream itself credits OCRmyPDF and PaddleOCR; see README.md.
